00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Beriya 50-60 salî ewan jî çûn derve xwendin.
 
50-60 years ago they also went outside to study.

151
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Û xêr û xêratan. Yanî pir musaqef fîna, pir waî hene.
 
And so on. Meaning there are very educated ones, very aware
ones.

152
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Dêkên me, se'yê, nexwendavan bûn, bes dêkên me waî bûn ji bo
xwendinê.
 
Our mothers, initially, were uneducated, but our mothers
were aware about studying.

153
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Digotin, "Bila qîzkên me bixwînin."
 
They said, "Let our daughters study."

154
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Pir rehet bûn didîtin. Qîzkên xwe dişandin Heleb, dişandin
Efrîn,
 
They were very comfortable seeing it. They sent their
daughters to Aleppo, they sent them to Afrin,

155
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:54,000
nanê gund, xwarinê gund da em nandin, bi gemeşeyan, bi
çiyê... îdare dikirin ji wan re.
 
village bread, village food they gave to send, with
vehicles, with things... they managed for them.

156
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Û ruxmî kalên me, nexwendavan bûn, dîsa tedhiye dikirin.
 
And despite our elders being uneducated, they still made
sacrifices.

157
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Digotin "Silahekî xweş e di destê qîzkên me de be."
 
They said, "It is a good weapon to be in the hands of our
daughters."

158
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
"Ê di tengiyê de xwe xelas kin."
 
"So they can save themselves in hardships."

159
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Ev xwendekar niha gişt li gund in, yan na?
 
Are all these students in the village now, or not?

160
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Hin li derve ne,
 
Some are abroad,

161
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:10,000
hin li gund in, hin li Helebê ne, heryek li welatekî ye.
 
some are in the village, some are in Aleppo, each is in a
country.

162
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Mesela, Doktor Xelîl,
 
For example, Doctor Khalil,

163
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Doktor Xelîl, ew jî însanekî siyasî, pir pak bû, rewşenbîr
bû.
 
Doctor Khalil, he was also a political person, very pure, he
was an intellectual.

164
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Ew jî li derve ye. Em jî xwe qat nekir, li nav da,
 
He is also abroad. We didn't fold ourselves, inside,

165
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Ji esbabê herba û tiştan, rabû çû derve. Neta zane.
 
Because of the war and things, he got up and went abroad. As
you know.

166
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Ev nav gişt li derve ne.
 
All these people are abroad.

167
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Ê ka tu kanî behsa komîn û nekomînan... hûn çi karî dikin?
Ku mesela tu niha li vê derê li gund e.
 
So can you talk about the communes and non-communes... what
work do you do? Since for example you are now here in the
village.

168
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Tê sibê radibî, çi kar heye, çi tine ye?
 
When you wake up in the morning, what work is there, what is
not?

169
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Welleh, karê min...
 
Well, my work...

170
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Karê min, ez xizmeta mala xwe dikim. Bavikê xwe.
 
My work, I serve my home. My father.

171
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Dêkê min rehma Xwedê kir, ez xizmetê dikim.
 
My mother passed away, I serve.

172
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Û te zanî her, tu kar li derve tune ye, ti qîz ku daketin
Efrînê, kar tune bûn.
 
And you know every, there is no work outside, any girl that
went down to Afrin, there were no jobs.

173
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Heta ji aliye xwendinê de me newêrî.
 
Even regarding studying, we didn't dare.

174
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,000
Temam?
 
Right?

175
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
Ê birayê min, mesela, niha ku daket,
 
And my brother, for example, now that he went down,

176
00:13:49,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Va em muhesar bûn. Diwê milkê me çi jê dihat, me îdare
dikir.
 
Look, we were besieged. Whatever came from our property, we
managed with it.

177
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Belê, temaşevanên me yên hêja, niha em hatin mala Apê Ebû
Tilo,
 
Yes, our dear viewers, we have now come to the house of
Uncle Abu Tilo,

178
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,000
ew muxtarê gundê Keferdelê ya Jorîn e.
 
he is the mukhtar of the village of Upper Keferdelê.

179
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Em niha hatin ji ber ku em behsa gund bikin,
 
We came now to talk about the village,

180
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:46,000
tiştên ku ferin, li ser gund zanibin, dîroka vê gundî.
 
the things that are necessary, to know about the village,
the history of this village.

181
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Destpêkê, silav û rêz ji bo te, Apê Ebû Tilo.
 
First of all, greetings and respects to you, Uncle Abu Tilo.

182
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Spas ji we re, û hûn bi xêr hatin.
 
Thank you, and welcome.

183
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Ez dixwazim, behsa gund bikim.
 
I want to talk about the village.

184
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Ser dîroka gund ti biaxivî...
 
Talk about the history of the village...

185
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Ji malbatên eşîrên vê gundî, çawa bûn?
 
How were the families and tribes of this village?

186
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Beriya 500 salî. Çawa gund hate avakirin?
 
500 years ago. How was the village built?

187
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Kî malbatan, ev navdar li vê derê bû?
 
Which families were famous here?

188
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Ev gund, gundekî kevnar e.
 
This village is an ancient village.

189
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Dîroka vê gundî, li ser nexşeyê, li ser kevirên kevn, belkî
1170.
 
The history of this village, on the map, on the old stones,
maybe 1170.

190
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Ev gund ava bû.
 
This village was built.

191
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:27,000
Eyla Silef, eyla Hisên Bekîr...
 
The Silef family, the Hissen Bekir family...

192
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Axayên dîtir, malbatên axayên dîtira,
 
Other aghas, the families of other aghas,

193
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:37,000
Ê dudiya, malbata mala Elî.
 
The second, the family of Ali.

194
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Ê sisiya, malbata Şi'a...
 
The third, the Shia family...

195
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Jê re dibêjin Şi'ar.
 
They call them Shi'ar.

196
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Ê çara, malbata mala Teke.
 
The fourth, the Teke family.

197
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Û gundekî bi nav û deng e di xwendina xwe...
 
And it is a famous village in its education...

198
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Û di zanabûna xwe.
 
And in its knowledge.

199
00:15:54,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Xwendavan, ê ku niha em ji te re bêjin mamoste Tewsilef, ê
yekê ye.
 
Educated ones, the one we can mention now is teacher
Tewsilef, he is the first.

200
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,000
Belkî li Kurdaxê, li Çiyayê Kurmênc... ê sisiya bû.
 
Maybe in Kurd Dagh, in the Kurmanc Mountain... he was the
third.

201
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Dido wekî wî hebûn, ew jî ê sisiya ye.
 
There were two like him, and he was the third.

202
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Ustad Heyder Mihemed Genco.
 
Master Haydar Mihemed Genco.

203
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Dibistana vê gundî,
 
The school of this village,

204
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:17,000
sala 1947'an...
 
the year 1947...

205
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Dibistan ava kir.
 
The school was built.

206
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Kê dibistan çêkir? Bi nefsê xwe ava kir?
 
Who built the school? Did he build it himself?

207
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Apê min... Mamoste Heyder.
 
My uncle... Teacher Haydar.

208
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Em ê behsa bîrên avê bikin.
 
We will talk about the water wells.

209
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Li ser bîrên ku di axivî, li vê derê,
 
About the wells you talk about, here,

210
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
te gotibû bîrek galekî kevnar heye.
 
you said there is a very ancient well.

211
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Heye.
 
There is.

212
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Bîr ev li bakurê gund e.
 
This well is in the north of the village.

213
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Ji dema Rûman de.
 
From the Roman era.

214
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Dema Rûman de, ev bîra av jê dihat.
 
In the Roman era, water came from this well.

215
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Belkî gund û belkî gundên derdora wê, ji ava jê dibirin.
 
Maybe the village and maybe the surrounding villages took
water from it.

216
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Heya niha?
 
Until now?

217
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Niha bîrên din hene. Bîrên din her kesî bîrek ji xwe re
çêkiriye, û xezanên avê ji xwe re çêkirine.
 
Now there are other wells. For the other wells, everyone has
made a well for themselves, and they have made water tanks
for themselves.

218
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Heya niha ev e... berdayî ye, û kes av nakşîne.
 
Until now it is... abandoned, and no one draws water.

219
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Ka em vegerin destpêkê.
 
Let's go back to the beginning.

220
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Miletê vê gundî çi kar dikir?
 
What did the people of this village do for work?

221
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Tu zanî ev gundî, gundî ne, sewalan xwedî dikin.
 
You know these villagers, they are villagers, they keep
livestock.

222
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Wek miyan, wek çêlikan, wek bizinan.
 
Like sheep, like cows, like goats.

223
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Ne tu tiştên din cem wan hene? Feqet xwedî dikin?
 
Do they not have anything else? They only raise (livestock)?

224
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Ji ber guzeranê... jiyan bibin.
 
For the sake of livelihood... to live.

225
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Darên li vê derê? Em kanin bibêjin darên çi hene? Xeyrî
darên zeytûnê?
 
The trees here? What trees can we say there are? Other than
olive trees?

226
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Darên fêkî jî hene.
 
There are also fruit trees.

227
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Wek?
 
Like?

228
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Wek hejîra,
 
Like fig,

229
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
wek gûza,
 
like walnut,

230
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,000
wek sêvan,
 
like apples,

231
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:50,000
û mêw jî hene, mêwên tirî.
 
and there are also vines, grape vines.

232
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Û belê, mişmiş ji...
 
And yes, apricots too...

233
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Mişmiş jî hene.
 
There are apricots too.

234
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Fêkî gelek hene, reng bi reng hene.
 
There are many fruits, in various colors.

235
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Aliyê hunerî, ez biçûk bûm,
 
On the artistic side, when I was small,

236
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:05,000
yek li gund hebû, jê re digotin Mihemedê Elî Bedel.
 
there was one in the village, they called him Mihemed Ali
Bedel.

237
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Bi saetan...
 
For hours...

238
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Bi şevan digotin.
 
At nights they would tell.

239
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:13,000
Hem çîrok, û hem bi deng.
 
Both stories, and with voice (singing).

240
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:17,000
Yanî dewlemend bû. Bi peyv û gotinên xwe.
 
Meaning he was rich. With his words and sayings.

241
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Û yekî din hebû, çîrokvan bû,
 
And there was another, he was a storyteller,

242
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
jê re digotin Sebrî Hisên.
 
they called him Sebri Hisen.

243
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:29,000
Çîrokvan bû, ji êvar dest pê dikir û ber destê sibê xelas
dibû çîrok.
 
He was a storyteller, he would start in the evening and by
the morning the story would be finished.

244
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Heya niha hene?
 
Are they still here?

245
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Êdî niha, tu kes nemaye. Ewan zû de, ez zarok bûm.
 
Now, no one is left. That was long ago, I was a child.

246
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Ev tiştan min didîtin.
 
I saw these things.

247
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:41,000
Em dikarin bibêjin 1961'an agirekî Newrozê,
 
We can say in 1961 a Newroz fire,

248
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:44,000
li Çiyayê Kurmênc li gundê me, çêbû.
 
in the Kurmanc Mountain in our village, happened.

249
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Û bi sedema wê cejna Newrozê,
 
And because of that Newroz celebration,

250
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
21'ê Adarê,
 
March 21st,

251
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:52,000
li defê xistin û dîlan çêkirin.
 
they played the daf and danced.

252
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Kîjan salê de?
 
In which year?

253
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:57,000
1961.
 
1961.

254
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Em ê behsa siyaseta gund bikin.
 
We will talk about the politics of the village.

255
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Yanî pirkên partî li vê derê hebûn? Ku kanî hinekî behsa wan
bikî?
 
Were there many parties here? Can you talk a bit about them?

256
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Bi xwedê ev gund,
 
By God, this village,

257
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:11,000
da ez biçûk bûm, ev nav wanda mezin bûm.
 
when I was small, I grew up among them.

258
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
Partî çêbûn.
 
Parties were formed.

259
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Ê evwilî,
 
The first,

260
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
P.D.K. Sûriyê.
 
P.D.K. Syria.

261
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Ê ewilî, Ustaz Xelîl Ebdullah. Xelîl Mihemed Ebdullah.
 
The first, Master Khalil Abdullah. Khalil Mihemed Abdullah.

262
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:29,000
Ew ji bingehê wan bû, ji esasê... ji esasên partî.
 
He was from their foundation, from the base... from the
foundations of the party.

263
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Û Kemal Ebdî,
 
And Kemal Abdi,

264
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:35,000
ew jî xwarzê gundê me ye û pismamê me ye,
 
he is also a nephew of our village and our cousin,

265
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:38,000
û Hesen Ebdurehman Kenco.
 
and Hasan Abdurrahman Kenco.

266
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Me got, evan...
 
We said, these...

267
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Evan... partîna...
 
These... parties...

268
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Li hev civîn.
 
Gathered together.

269
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Û di sala 1961'an agirê Newrozê pê xistin.
 
And in the year 1961 they lit the Newroz fire.

270
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Çima? Lianne komîteya wan a bilind...
 
Why? Because their high committee...

271
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
gihîştin zîndanê.
 
reached the prison.

272
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Wan jî xwastin, ji bo rûmeta wan...
 
They also wanted, for their honor...

273
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:04,000
... an gû, ey jinan divê em tiştên wilo agir pêdixist.
 
... or ..., oh women, we used to light such things on fire.

274
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
..agir pêdixistin.
 
..we lit fires.

275
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:10,000
em ji 20ê mehê da em agir pêdixistin,
 
we would light fires from the 20th of the month,

276
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:15,000
bila bibînin, Kurd namirin, û partî namire.
 
so they can see, Kurds don't die, and the party doesn't die.

277
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Jiber vê yekê agirekî Newrozê şeva 21ê
 
Because of this, a Newroz fire on the night of the 21st,

278
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:26,000
yanî şeva 21ê yanî 20ê adarê bi şev, saet 6an agir pêxistin.
 
meaning the night of the 21st, meaning the night of the 20th
of March, at 6 o'clock, they lit a fire.

279
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,000
û bû sibe
 
and morning came,

280
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
def û dildar çêkirin û...
 
they prepared drums and zurna and...

281
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:34,000
hol lêxistin û... cejna xwe kirin.
 
danced the halay and... celebrated their festival.

282
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Di du wan ra pirr êş û keder kişandin.
 
After that they suffered a lot of pain and sorrow.

283
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
wek.. zindanan da, alem digirtin..
 
like.. in prisons, they arrested everyone..

284
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:47,000
heya.. emrê wî 13 û 14 digirtin, heya yê emrê wî 75 û 80..
 
they arrested even those aged 13 and 14, up to those aged 75
and 80..

285
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,000
ha wina digirtin û.. dikirin zindanan.
 
they arrested them like that and.. put them in prisons.

286
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:54,000
bi vê... îfade û tişt.. û bi vê dînikirinê..
 
with this... statement and stuff.. and with this madness..

287
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:58,000
hema bes ji Keferdelê ba.. xilas.
 
as long as they were from Keferdele.. that's it.

288
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:02,000
bes ji Keferdelê ba.. navê wî ji Keferdelê ba (digotin)
yalla were.
 
as long as they were from Keferdele.. if their name was from
Keferdele, (they'd say) come on.

289
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:06,000
..naha.. ji wan ew mirin..
 
..now.. those people have died..

290
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:09,000
û ew zulm û zora.. nema.
 
and that oppression and tyranny.. is gone.

291
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:29,000
û hat guhertin..
 
and it changed..

292
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:43,000
Ev şikeft e, pirr kevn e, pirr.
 
This is a cave, very old, very.

293
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,000
Kesek nizane kê hazir kirîbû.
 
No one knows who prepared it.

294
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:52,000
Li vir.. li derê hanê wekî haziriyek çêkirîbû.. yek quncik
xwarin çêdikî.
 
Here.. in this place, they prepared it like a settlement.. a
corner for cooking.

295
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:57,000
Li derê hanê.. yek xizan hebû.. pirr malê wî tinne bû..
 
In this place.. there was a poor man.. he didn't have much
property..

296
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:00,000
Dihat li vê derê, xew dikir.. xwarin çêdikir, û vedixwar,
tişt dikirin...
 
He would come here, sleep.. cook, and drink, do things...

297
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Betaybetî zivistanê...
 
Especially in the winter...

298
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Xêr e, vir zivistanê germ e.. û havînê hênik e... wek te dî
naha.
 
It's good, here it's warm in winter.. and cool in summer...
like you see now.

299
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:14,000
Li derê hanê keçik dilîstin...
 
In this place, little girls would play...

300
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,000
Mebesta te li vir...
 
You mean here...

301
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Li derê hanê.. bi gulo dilîstin.
 
In this place.. they played with marbles.

302
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,000
qeçkên çûçik..
 
little kids..

303
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,000
Li derê wê da,
 
In that place,

304
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:26,000
ên mezin.. bi îskembîlê dilîzin, dizanim..
 
the older ones.. play cards, I know..

305
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:32,000
adet.. adetên gundan.. yanî.. nas nakin.. hella bi tiştekî
xwe meşxûl dibin.
 
traditions.. village traditions.. I mean.. they don't know
each other.. they just keep busy with something.

306
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:34,000
Ev kîjan salan bû?
 
What years were these?

307
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Bixwedê ez biçûk bûm.
 
By God, I was little.

308
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:39,000
ez sefê didwê sêyê bûm.. ez dihatim vê derê..
 
I was in the second, third grade.. I would come here..

309
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:44,000
û heta gihiştim sefê 7ê û 8ê.. ez dîsa dihatimê..
 
and until I reached seventh and eighth grade.. I still
came..

310
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:47,000
zivistanê.. sar dibû.. me ra.. tiştek nebû yanî.
 
in the winter.. it would be cold.. we didn't have any
problem.

311
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:50,000
Yanî şikeft zivistanan germ, havînan hênik?
 
So the cave is warm in winter, cool in summer?

312
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Pirr, pirr! Mora em mesrefê bikî..
 
Very much, very! Why would we spend money..

313
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:58,000
tekiyê zingo û sobeyê deynî û derxî û pexarî.. berê pexarî
bûn li malan.
 
setting up stoves and chimneys and stuff.. there used to be
chimneys in houses.

314
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Vê derê.. ev tişt...
 
Here.. these things...

315
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
Tenê fêstanek dihat lixwekirin?
 
Only a dress was worn?

316
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Belê.. yek ewê xwe tenê hebû, zivistanê fêstan lê dikirin.
 
Yes.. one just had this, they wore dresses in winter.

317
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Fêstan bes..
 
Just a dress..

318
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Eh.. dihat vê derê germ..
 
Yeah.. they would come here, it was warm..

319
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:17,000
berf li erdê.. bi ka bikî.. berf li erdê, tu dihatî vê
derê.. germ.. tişt dikin eger germ e.
 
snow on the ground.. what can you do.. snow on the ground,
you come here.. it's warm.. they do things if it's warm.

320
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Belê.. Navê vê şikeftê çî ye?
 
Yes.. What is the name of this cave?

321
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Vê re dibêjin.. şikefta Ga..
 
They call it.. the Ox Cave..

322
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
Çêlek...
 
Cow...

323
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Çima navê Ga lê hatiye kirin?
 
Why was it named Ox?

324
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
Ga.. û çêlek...
 
Ox.. and cow...

325
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:30,000
xwedî dikirin.. pirr...
 
they raised.. a lot...

326
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
tişkî pirranî..
 
mostly things..

327
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:35,000
dikirin vê derê..
 
they put them here..

328
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Kê xwedî dikir?
 
Who raised them?

329
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:43,000
Herkeskî.. te heywanan dudu.. sê.. e min.. sê, çar, pênc..
didan kirin vê derê..
 
Everyone.. you have two.. three animals.. I have.. three,
four, five.. they would bring them and put them here..

330
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:45,000
Ez dixwazim.. hinekî behsa..
 
I want to.. talk a little about..

331
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:47,000
dîroka şikeftê bikim..
 
the history of the cave..

332
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:51,000
destpêkê kî hat.. vê şikeftê? Vê şikefta kî bir? kî tê da
rûnişt?
 
who came first.. to this cave? Who occupied this cave? Who
sat in it?

333
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:53,000
Û beriya çend salan?
 
And how many years ago?

334
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:59,000
Eh.. ev dewro silav, ew hatin.. bapîrên me.. Mala Qedûr.
 
Uh.. our ancestors.. the Qedûr family.

335
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Mala Qedûr?
 
The Qedûr family?

336
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:02,000
Erê Mala Qedûr hatin.. vê derê.
 
Yes, the Qedûr family came.. here.

337
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Û du birak bûn..
 
And they were two brothers..

338
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:08,000
Mehmed, Bekir,
 
Mehmed, Bekir,

339
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:12,000
Bekir axa digotin û... Mehmed axa.
 
They called him Bekir Agha and... Mehmed Agha.

340
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:16,000
Ev parî ya e ma, e mala Mehmed axa... ev parî din ê mala
Bekir axa..
 
This part was ours, Mehmed Agha's family... the other part
was Bekir Agha's family..

341
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:21,000
Û ev çiqas sal, em nizanin.. ev.. hazir bû.
 
And how many years this has been here, we don't know.. it..
was ready.

342
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:24,000
yanî navê wê çêkir..
 
I mean, whoever built it..

343
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Ji berê da ye.
 
It's from long ago.

344
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:26,000
erê ji berê da ye...
 
Yes, it's from long ago...

345
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Belkî cîhekî weye, (caşikan lê vedikirin).. cihek.. heye..
li derva heye.
 
Maybe it's a place of theirs, (where they tied donkeys).. a
place.. there is.. outside there is.

346
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:34,000
Em ê li we bibînin .. dîroka wê derê.. ko bo tişt dikirin.
 
We will see there .. the history of that place.. where they
did things.

347
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:38,000
Zehmetî li vir tinne bû? Jiber ku av tinne ye.
 
Was there no difficulty here? Because there is no water.

348
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:39,000
Na.. av heye...
 
No.. there is water...

349
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Ciyê avê dûr e?
 
Is the water place far?

350
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:43,000
Ciyê avê.. na ne dûr e, ne dûr e, vê derê..
 
The water place.. no it's not far, not far, here..

351
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:46,000
û herkesekî ji xwe re filaqek (fireqek) tişt girtin û...
xwedî dikirin.. ji bo heywanan av daxin derê din ..
 
and everyone took a bucket for themselves and... they
raised.. they took water down for the animals to the other
side..

352
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Yanî li vir xwedî dikirin û rûdiniştin.
 
So they raised them here and sat down.

353
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Na herkes şikeftek heye...
 
No, everyone has a cave...

354
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:55,000
Belkî 20 şikeft hene, bes ne wek vê..
 
Maybe there are 20 caves, but not like this one..

355
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:57,000
Eh çûktir...
 
Uh, smaller...

356
00:24:57,000 --> 00:25:03,000
Lê wek ku me bihîstiye, destpêkê, malbata we hatine li vir
derê, kesekî... hatine Gund... mal tine bû.. Hatin şikeftê
da rûniştin.
 
But as we heard, at first, your family came here, someone...
came to the village... there were no houses.. They came to
the cave and sat.

357
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:07,000
Eh, şikefta da.. erê, belê, rast e.
 
Uh, in the cave.. yes, yes, that's right.

358
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:10,000
Nimûne.. dibên... şikefta Şeho..
 
For example.. they say... Şeho's cave..

359
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:13,000
yekî.. navî xwe Şeha bû...
 
someone.. his name was Şeha...

360
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:22,000
hat li vê derê, vê jê re digotin şikefta Şeho, hat li vê
derê. Û li şikeftê da, ma...
 
came here, they called it Şeho's cave, he came here. And
stayed in the cave...

361
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:28,000
Naha.. faydeya vê şikeftê.. ko em bêjin... piştî tetawurê...
bûn mal û avahî li vê derê.. weke em naha dibînin..
 
Now.. the benefit of this cave.. let's say... after
development... houses and buildings were built here.. as we
see now..

362
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:31,000
Çi faydeya xwe heye li ser... xelkê gund?
 
What benefit does it have for... the village people?

363
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:35,000
Ser xelkê gund? Niha tînin vê derê.. dewarên xwe..
 
For the village people? Now they bring their cattle here..

364
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:37,000
Xelkê gund tînin.. an ewên derdorê xwe..
 
The village people bring.. or those from the surroundings..

365
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Ew derdorê xwe. Tînin li vê derê, vê jê ra tiştan bigire li
mal û derva ke, vê derê.. tiştî sar û kû..
 
Those from the surroundings. They bring them here, take this
grass or things and take them outside the house, here.. cold
things and deep..

366
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Ev alavên min, dev û alavên min.. çeltîk, çember, misk û
enber.. toza berber.. hincik-mincik.. libbê çûçik...
 
These tools of mine, tools and equipment.. paddy, hoop, musk
and amber.. barber's powder.. odds and ends.. little
sparrow..

367
00:25:56,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Ev alavên min dev û alavên min... çeltîk û çember... çeltîk
û çember çi ye?
 
These tools of mine... paddy and hoop... what is paddy and
hoop?

368
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:05,000
Berê bazirganî çêdibû, bi çeltîk û çember.
 
In the past there was trade, with paddy and hoops.

369
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:10,000
Çeltîk, riz.. Çember, tiştî tên firotanê ji bajar dihatin...
 
Paddy, rice.. Hoop, things to sell came from the city...

370
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:13,000
çi danîn.. misk û enber..
 
what they brought.. musk and amber..

371
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:16,000
Ava bêhna xweş dihatin. Toza berber...
 
Good smelling waters came. Barber's powder...

372
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:23,000
dema te.. yek.. seriyê xwe çêkir.. çû cem berber toza tê
didin.. erê..
 
when you.. did your hair.. you went to the barber, they put
powder on it.. right..

373
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Hincik-mincik... hincik, por e.. serî ye... ev seriyê min
filan û bêvan e, tişt e..
 
Odds and ends... hair.. head... my head is this and that,
things..

374
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:32,000
Tiştên wina...
 
Things like that...

375
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:39,000
Tiştên di wana de rêz dikin.. û te digot.. toza berber..
hincik û mincik... libbê çûçik.
 
Things they arrange in them.. and you said.. barber's
powder.. odds and ends... sparrow grain.

376
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:45,000
Lebbeyke ya tifl. Bi erebî ye yanî.. libbê çûçik.
 
Lebbeyke ya tifl. It's Arabic.. sparrow grain.

377
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:54,000
çûçik (çîçik) dilîstin... qeçê meçê helqêçê.. qereqûtiq fêş
parçik..
 
they played sparrow... qeçê meçê helqêçê.. qereqûtiq fêş
parçik..

378
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:56,000
gî peyvin û maneyên xwe hene.
 
They are all words and have their meanings.

379
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Çend salî bû te ev dilîstin..
 
How old were you when you played these..

380
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Bi xwedê ez 8-10 salî bûm wiha...
 
By God I was 8-10 years old like this...

381
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:07,000
Bes a wê digotin, pisê, pisê, keçeke.. ev yê keçekê ye...
pisê, pisê,
 
But they said that one, cat, cat, it's a girl's.. this one
is for a girl... cat, cat,

382
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:08,000
dûv me qesê,
 
after us cut,

383
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:11,000
kef û girgir, bane mirgir...
 
foam and round, flat roof round...

384
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:16,000
Mêr hecî ye, kew kûştî ye, para pisê nehiştî ye.
 
The man is a pilgrim, the partridge is killed, the cat's
share is left.

385
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:19,000
Hebu heta naha jî hene..
 
They existed, even now they exist..

386
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:23,000
Em ê niha bixwazin ji vir derkevin...
 
We would like to leave from here now...

387
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:27,000
Ne ji vir derket... em Kurd kevnar in.
 
Don't leave from here... we Kurds are ancient.

388
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:47,000
Bi siruştê..
 
In nature..

389
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:03,000
Belê.. temaşevanên me yên hêja...
 
Yes.. our dear viewers...

390
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Naha em derbasî mala kê bûn... li gundê Keferdelê ya jorî?
 
Now whose house have we entered... in the upper Keferdele
village?

391
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:08,000
Ev mal...
 
This house...

392
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:10,000
Gelek tiştên dîrokî lê hene.
 
There are many historical things in it.

393
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:13,000
Tiştên ji dîroka Efrînê, û bi taybetî ji dîroka vî gundî.
 
Things from the history of Afrin, and especially from the
history of this village.

394
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:17,000
Em ê pê re derbas bibin, ka em ê binêrin, ev tiştane çine...
 
We will go through it, let's see, what are these things...

395
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:19,000
Û mêvanê me li vê derê heye...
 
And our guest is here...

396
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Ew ê.. ji me re.. bibêje.
 
She will.. tell us.

397
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:23,000
Merheba Xaltîkê...
 
Hello Auntie...

398
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:26,000
Ehlan we sehlan, ser çavan.. hatina we xêr.. ser serê me..
 
Welcome, on the eyes.. your arrival is good.. on our heads..

399
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:27,000
Bi xêr hatin..
 
Welcome..

400
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:28,000
Navê te xêr?
 
May your name be good?

401
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:29,000
Sedîqea Osman Bekir.
 
Sediqea Osman Bekir.

402
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Temenê te?
 
Your age?

403
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,000
62...
 
62...

404
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:33,000
Xaltîka min em hatin vê derê..
 
My aunt, we came here..

405
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,000
Ehlen we sehlen..
 
Welcome..

406
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:36,000
me dît gelek tiştên dîrokî di cem te hene..
 
we saw you have many historical things with you..

407
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:37,000
tiştên kevnar..
 
ancient things..

408
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,000
belê, erê..
 
yes, yes..

409
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:41,000
tiştên xas.. ji dîroka Efrînê ye.. ji kelepora Efrînê ye...
 
special things.. from the history of Afrin.. from the
heritage of Afrin...

410
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:43,000
ez dixwazim te ji me re... bibêjî, ev tiştên vê derê çine?
 
I want you to.. tell us, what are these things here?

411
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:47,000
E welleh.. dema berê, me sebir.. nan dikir.
 
Well.. in the old days, we had patience.. made bread.

412
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Bes naha nan hazir e. Naxwe ne heyirin, dar nayênin, tînin.
 
But now bread is ready. They don't tire themselves, they
don't bring wood, they bring it.

413
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:55,000
Û ev makîne.. destan.. berê.. me heywan lê diqestan, kufte
dikirin..
 
And this hand machine.. in the past.. we minced meat in it,
made meatballs..

414
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:57,000
ev makîne..
 
this machine..

415
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Û teb'en ev çira na jî berê.. tiştê em pê dixistin.. li
berê...
 
And of course these lamps also in the past.. the thing we
lit with.. in the past...

416
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:03,000
An anîna qereman an qeştûran... me tiştên qerem rokirin...
berê bo çaranîna qezancê qey? Çira?
 
Or bringing pots, or cauldrons... We saw the pots being
emptied... In the past, was it for earning a living? A lamp?

417
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Çira, erê, erê. 4 nimre ye, erê.
 
A lamp, yes, yes. It's a size 4, yes.

418
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:08,000
Weha bû, cîyê misîn, berê henefiyat tune bûn...
 
That's how it was, instead of copper pitchers, there were no
faucets in the past...

419
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:12,000
Ev misîn em pê av didan... em pê nivînên xwe paqij dikirin,
zarokên xwe pê li ber dişûştin, der dikirin...
 
We used this copper pitcher to pour water... we used it to
clean our beds, we washed our children with it, we cleaned
with it...

420
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:14,000
Ji çi ye ev misîn e? Nuhas e?
 
What is this copper pitcher made of? Copper?

421
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:15,000
Nuhas e, erê nuhas e.
 
Copper, yes it's copper.

422
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Ev qunc in, berê em rûn tê dikirin... me tê da rûn dikirin.
 
These are jugs, we used to put butter in them... we put
butter in them.

423
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:20,000
Niha qa rûnê nika tune ye.
 
Now, there's no such butter like there used to be.

424
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Wan pê dizanin çi dikin, me dixiya, me der dikir... me çi
dikir...
 
They know what they do with it, we used to churn it, we took
it out... we did whatever...

425
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:27,000
Ev dergûş e, me berê evî, me qîçkê xwe tê da mezin dikirin.
 
This is a cradle, we used to, we raised our babies in it.

426
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:29,000
Nika modeyên dergûşan neman.
 
Now the fashion of cradles is gone.

427
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:32,000
Dikirin... der dikirin, hildikirin...
 
They put them in... they took them out, they lifted them...

428
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:38,000
Ev qolinc in... genim diçandin, me diçû ye... mêrên me,
qîçkên me... em pê diçiniyan, paleyî... genim.
 
These are sickles... they planted wheat, we used to go...
our husbands, our children... we harvested with it,
harvesting... wheat.

429
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:40,000
Ev meqes in, me pê dirûn dikir...
 
These are scissors, we used to sew with them...

430
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:41,000
We pê dikir lê niha?
 
You used to do it with them, but now?

431
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:44,000
Na, ê niha, êdî xeyat hene, derzin hene, kes bi ya xwe da
naşîne.
 
No, now, there are tailors, there are sewing machines, no
one bothers to do it themselves.

432
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:47,000
Bes ev dibîsim... lingên we, heta niha... evana hin?
 
But I hear this... your legs, until now... are these still
here?

433
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:50,000
E ha ne, hene, ez ê lengo nebim, ev êdî lengo...
 
Here they are, they are here, I shouldn't be crippled, these
are for the legs...

434
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Mêrkên lengo, bo pê... bo destan bo pê... ne?
 
Men's leg bands, for the feet... for hands, for feet...
right?

435
00:30:54,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Ev pê ra, ev... birûş... berxur bû, me tije berxur
dikirin... me berxur dicalan, tije berxur... cewalî berxur
in.
 
This with it, this... bulgur pot... it was for bulgur, we
filled it with bulgur... we stored bulgur, full of bulgur...
sacks of bulgur.

436
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:02,000
Tije berxur, cewalî berxur.
 
Full of bulgur, sacks of bulgur.

437
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Ê niha diherin bi kîloyan dikirin, xwa nuh heyran, wekî me
xwa rehet nakin.
 
Now they go and buy it by the kilos, my dear, they don't
bother making themselves comfortable like us.

438
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:10,000
Ev paşna... me tê da dims dicalan, dimsê hinar, dimsê şêrîn.
 
This heel... we stored molasses in it, pomegranate molasses,
sweet molasses.

439
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:13,000
Ê nika, giyê bo hawana... ev nika ev e?
 
And now, all for this mortar... this one here?

440
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Na, ev... ev moleg e...
 
No, this... this is a pestle...

441
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Moleg e, an jî...
 
A pestle, or...

442
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:19,000
Erê, moleg e, jî hene... û ev elek, me pê ard dibêt...
 
Yes, it's a pestle, there are also... and this sieve, we
sifted flour with it...

443
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:23,000
Ev navê, me pê dan dikelan, dan, doxê danya... hildidan,
dikeliyan...
 
This in it, we boiled wheat with it, wheat, bulgur wheat...
they took it, boiled it...

444
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:24,000
Jê... çi hildidan, daxistin?
 
From it... what did they take, put down?

445
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Nika... nika deran bi bîra derdixin...
 
Now... now they take things out with a well...

446
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:28,000
Qey, ev navên tenen, nika.
 
Right, there are none of these names now.

447
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Ê ev nav... îştê ev legen e, me tê da hevîr distiran.
 
And this name... see, this is a basin, we kneaded dough in
it.

448
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,000
Ev legen e, me tê da hevîr distiran.
 
This is a basin, we kneaded dough in it.

449
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:35,000
Bêjing e, bêjing e...
 
It's a sieve, it's a sieve...

450
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:37,000
Bêjing e, kî ye ev? Oho, ev bêjing...
 
It's a sieve, what is this? Oh, this sieve...

451
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:40,000
Me pê nîsk dibêtan, me pê genim dibêtan...
 
We sifted lentils with it, we sifted wheat with it...

452
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Li ser bîdarê.
 
On the threshing floor.

453
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:44,000
Ê nika ev modana giyê neman e.
 
Now all these fashions are gone.

454
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Ev kovar jina ne, berê...?
 
Is this a women's magazine, from the past...?

455
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:47,000
Ê, karê jinê berê... ne ev nav.
 
Yes, women's work in the past... not these things.

456
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:52,000
Bes, nika... jinên nika got, qolên wan na... dikin, evna
dindir e, û şîvê da qesî xozanan e.
 
But, now... women of today say, their arms don't... work,
these are fastides, and their meals are just scraps.

457
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Am li ber... pxurî dibûn, am li ber...
 
We used to be covered in dust in front of... we used to be
in front of...

458
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:56,000
Ku em giştan bidin... em dixwazin...
 
When we give them all... we want to...

459
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:58,000
...bahsa jinan bikin.
 
...talk about women.

460
00:31:58,000 --> 00:32:00,000
Karê jinan... berê, çawa bû? Nika çawa bû?
 
Women's work... in the past, how was it? How is it now?

461
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:02,000
Ê, nika, ah.
 
Well, now, ah.

462
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Berê genim, destpê kir... e, kevin bikin. Paşê, werin li ser
çerxê...
 
In the past, wheat, started... uh, to make it old. Then,
come to the wheel...

463
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:10,000
Ê, berê me kito dikirin... li ser êr, me dolmeçek û
digermandin... li ser êr...
 
Well, in the past we made kito... over the fire, we warmed
dolmas... over the fire...

464
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:17,000
Me nan dikir li ser êr, me kinc dişikandin, xwesiya me lefa
û organ... gişt li ser êr dikelandin, nika gişt bîne xisala.
 
We baked bread over the fire, we washed clothes, our mother-
in-law's quilts and blankets... boiled them all over the
fire, now bring it all to the washing machine.

465
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:19,000
Kê pê qey dikin?
 
Who bothers doing it?

466
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Ê karê jinan berê...
 
Well, women's work in the past...

467
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:21,000
Hene.
 
Yes.

468
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:23,000
Ê derveyî malê jî evana dikanin kar bikin?
 
Well, outside the house, could they also work?

469
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:25,000
Dikirin... derveyî malê jî dikirin...
 
They did... outside the house they also did...

470
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Paleyî diçinin, gîsên diçinin, ê... diçûn mêrên xwe ra evro
dikirin, çi av... xumir...
 
Harvesting crops, cutting grass, uh... they went with their
husbands and did this, whatever water... dough...

471
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:36,000
Têr dikirin, xumir... genim. Diçinin, diçinin, dikin arde,
mêro diçinin, bo... bo qoluncan...
 
They fed them, dough... wheat. They harvest, harvest, turn
it into flour, men harvest, for... for the sickles...

472
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:41,000
Û jinan jî... ro dikir... dû ra ro dikir, didan hev... didan
hev, û didan...
 
And women too... poured... then poured it, gathered it...
gathered it, and gave...

473
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:47,000
Paşê... dikirin şeqr e... dar dikirin. Danî cerce rî dikir,
ev karê me zemanê tişt, ewî tişt... niha namîne.
 
Then... they turned it into a pile... they arranged the
sticks. They gathered it on the threshing machine, this is
our work from the time of things, that thing... doesn't
exist now.

474
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:49,000
Tiştek nema wiha çax...
 
Nothing is left from that time...

475
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:51,000
Tiştê berê, cîpî xopir bûn?
 
In the past, were there mud plows?

476
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:53,000
Welleh, me dikirin.
 
By God, we made them.

477
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:55,000
O... welleh min, ew bawermendên, wekî ku...
 
Oh... by God I, those believers, like...

478
00:32:55,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Em... me jarcar ji avkî... me paleyî jê kir, bi taştê, me
nan jê kir...
 
We... we watered the field with a tractor... we harvested
it, with breakfast, we baked bread from it...

479
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:07,000
Me dikir, me bostik ji jêr kir... wey wey... we ji ê
bêstiqa... bostikî, tere hejîro, li ser çarşefê, me
radixist...
 
We did it, we made bostik from the bottom... oh oh... from
the bastiq... bostik, fresh figs, on the sheet, we spread it
out...

480
00:33:07,000 --> 00:33:09,000
Û me avê ji... wekî malê, me dîz dikir...
 
And we took the water from... like the house, we made
pots...

481
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:13,000
Nika tu zanî heta nika... bostik, çê dikin?
 
Now do you know if until now... they make bostik?

482
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:20,000
Bo çi sa pê... bo bî bêstiq, li ser... ewê dikin... li ser
paçikên xwe dikin, ev bêjin ano, dîz dikin, ano. Dîz dikin.
 
What is it for... for making bastiq, on... they make it...
they make it on their cloths, they say this ano, they
arrange it, ano. They arrange it.

483
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:24,000
Pê dîz dikin... kuncîyan dirêşinin... reşreşikê, pê dirêşin
e...
 
They arrange it with it... they sprinkle sesame... black
seeds, they sprinkle it with it...

484
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:31,000
Ê, berê cira tune bû, ev pêlino... pê hîç de neveguharîn
deran, evê berê ne nîha. Nika hûn, elektrîk hene...
 
Well, in the past there was no electricity, these waves...
didn't change the places at all, this was in the past, not
now. Now you have electricity...

485
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Welleh no, ev ne tiştê berê ye, leza min... kes pê ihtîraf
nake... wekî ev tişt ne...
 
By God no, this is not a thing of the past, my haste... no
one confesses... like this thing is not...

486
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:36,000
Batarî dikafin e.
 
The batteries die.

487
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:38,000
Batarî dikafin e, erê...
 
The batteries die, yes...

488
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:47,000
Ê nika, ... ev... pê dav... dawe digerandin... pê ev... bi
zemanê berê, pê dawe digerandin...
 
Well now, ... this... thread... they spun thread... with
this... in the old days, they spun thread with it...

489
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Ev kevcino... me... pê dawe vedixwar, û noka pê va... noka
gişt kews e... delalê min, û ev va dexe...
 
These spoons... we... drank with them, and now with it...
now everything is plastic... my dear, and this...

490
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Dikirin... zerikê û kepkî pê dikan, girêdan pê dikan...
 
They did... they wore yellow beads and headpieces with it,
they wore headbands with it...

491
00:33:56,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Ê, nika, da şerba dale dixe. Nişk ji noka qolo yê bûye.
 
Well, now, they pour water from a pitcher. Suddenly now it
has become barren.

492
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Xaltîka min, ... cil û bergê te, gellekî xweş e ka...
 
My aunt, ... your clothes, are very beautiful, look...

493
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:05,000
Cil û bergê, rind e ka...
 
The clothes are beautiful, look...

494
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Kû cûmar bêje te ev kinco, ê kû derê ye?
 
Where did you get this from, where is this dress from?

495
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:13,000
Welleh ev kincê Efrîniya... ev kincê Efrînîya me bi xwe
raneyat.
 
By God, this is the dress of Afrin... this is the dress of
Afrin, we have it ourselves.

496
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:14,000
Te jê derê hazi...
 
You have it ready...

497
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:17,000
Ha, me hazir, derê çêkir... am pê çêdikin, cila am didin
Efrînî ne.
 
Yes, we have it ready, we made it... we make them with it,
we give clothes, we are from Afrin.

498
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Erê kurdê Efrînî ne.
 
Yes, the Kurds of Afrin.

499
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:19,000
Û şar pê... ser serî?
 
And the scarf with it... on the head?

500
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:24,000
Welleh ev... meşarê Efrînî ka rî? Ew jî rû Efrînî ka rî.
 
By God this... the scarf of Afrin, where is it? That too is
from Afrin, where is it.

501
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Me tiştê, dindît...
 
We saw, things...

502
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:28,000
Ê... berê dî... dibêjin, qenewîc...
 
Yes... in the past... they say, embroidery...

503
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Erê qenewîc.
 
Yes, embroidery.

504
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Erê qenewîc.
 
Yes, embroidery.

505
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Ev çawa, te çêkirin?
 
How did you make this?

506
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:39,000
Ê, berê wilo çêdikirin... berê, me ten ten çêdikir, qenewîç
çêdikirin, nika wa no çê nakin, ev ê me berê nen... me
rokirin a...
 
Well, in the past they made them like this... in the past,
we made lace, made embroidery, now they don't make them like
that, this is from our past... we passed them down...

507
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:40,000
Wê çû çêdikir, wê manî çi dibe?
 
What were you making, what does it mean?

508
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Me derge çêdikirin... me dikira li ser balgîya... balgîyê
dêrî, me merzin çêdikirin ji bûkor a... ji zavor a...
 
We made covers... we put them on pillows... door pillows, we
made blankets for the beds... for the children...

509
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:49,000
Ê, nika, we moda koşk tune a, rokiran a... çakirna... moden
xwedin da xistin a.
 
Well, now, that pavilion fashion is gone, they threw it
away... making... they laid out their own fashions.

510
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:52,000
Ê berê, me te pirca, perca we tişna di dî...
 
In the past, we spun your hair, we spun hair like this in
it...

511
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:53,000
Nika ev, digrin, cêze dibûko?
 
Now this, they take, bridal dowry?

512
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Dikirin cêze bûko.
 
They made bridal dowries.

513
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:55,000
Heta nika cêz...
 
Until now, the dowry...

514
00:34:55,000 --> 00:35:00,000
Noka? Çê nîne, na. Na... qet o dikin a. Cêzê bûko, gî...
hazir... le efrîntîn in.
 
Now? It doesn't exist, no. No... they don't do it at all.
The bridal dowry, all... ready... they buy them in Afrin.

515
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:02,000
Kesî, divan, qenah diki tune ye.
 
No one is satisfied with these.

516
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Çawa, xaltîk... jimar e... bêje te... wê resm e?
 
How, aunt... tell me... is that a picture?

517
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:13,000
Ê, we resm nû... ev rasm nû, me bo derzîya çêdikirî tişte...
wew jê xerbûcê ser a ye, di qulkî xerbûc o ro dikirin, û
derbaz dikirin.
 
Well, this picture is new... this new picture, we made it
with needles for things... and from the melon seeds on it,
they poured them into the hole of the melon, and passed them
through.

518
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Çavên me êş didîtin, me çêdikir. Ev jê bi mîl çêdikirin, ten
tene, mîl. B mîl çêdikirin.
 
Our eyes hurt, we made them. This was also made with a
knitting needle, lace, knitting needle. Made with a knitting
needle.

519
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:24,000
Em me kirin cehîzî qîziko, û lawko... diro... noka ev
modalêno gi tunen a. Bes ma tor a se... cam xos tina...
 
We made them as dowry for the girls, and boys... sewing...
now none of these fashions exist. But we just have net for
the... glass they like...

520
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:26,000
Çi xwa tixto xas tarakiran xellas kan?
 
Why do they throw away the special threads and finish them?

521
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:31,000
Yê heya yek e sa ro naşto, ê haya... çar û penç ro ye ha hef
to... ê daye me... am xîçik bûn am tunne ku sa ro naştiyo
no...
 
One throws it away, the one that... four or five days ago...
mother gave us... we were small, we weren't like the ones
that throw it away...

522
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:36,000
Make em çêdikirin, meş qîzkê xwer, qîzkê xwe ro çêdikirin...
şelko xore çêdikirin...
 
We used to make them, for our girls, we made them for our
girls... we made them for ourselves...

523
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:38,000
Ê da ista mal no kin no ko.
 
Well, now they don't do it in their homes.

524
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Noka gê, koşan a, gê deran a... gê tiştî hantika, derketi a.
Ne weha?
 
Now they are all mansions, all places... all antique things,
they have come out. Isn't that so?

525
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:47,000
Kê bi me çi... cefê berê, ma dîya kê sine dî? Qîçik la pişta
me bûn...
 
Who cares about us... the suffering of the past, who saw our
mother? Children were on our backs...

526
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:53,000
Waw am la ber taşte û nan, û kanco bûn... Cefê me, zike me
hayin mese ro wanki bî, amla bar taşta û qanco bûn.
 
And we were making breakfast and bread, and clothes... Our
suffering, our stomachs were hurting because of this, we
were making breakfast and clothes.

527
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Noka xesala dierxetena, qa cefî gê nû bin in...
 
Now they bring washing machines, so they are suffering from
a new kind of fatigue...

528
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:58,000
Me berê, cêfo pir dî...
 
In the past, we suffered a lot...

529
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:02,000
Me nan dikir, bteş to... heta cotyaro ma nan di dan, nan me
hazir a.
 
We baked bread, with dough... we gave bread to the plowman,
our bread was ready.

530
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:10,000
Paqijkî kinco ma dikiran... me nonî... bi qatir me bi zêytê
dara çêdikirin, dixwarin... we aklokûnî, pir xoş bî...
 
We cleaned the clothes... our bread... with a mule we made
olive oil with wood, they ate... that food, it was very
delicious...

531
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:13,000
Ê no ko karn a. Noni fîrne, nuni fîrnê, wakî bare di ba? Na.
 
Now they buy it. Bakery bread, bakery bread, is it like the
past? No.

532
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:17,000
Xwoşe, naahmeta... bes... tişti barê pir xoş bî... pir xoş
bî.
 
It's good, blessings... but... the things of the past were
very good... very good.

533
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Bi bi... gûluno... û ew a... bi barmîla zêt ro dirkirin, ne
ko dikan golûnîkî xwoşe kuxa. Sa qa çxoa? Xêr barê pir bî.
 
By the... buckets... and that... they poured oil into
barrels, now they say it's a good bucket. So what? The
blessings of the past were many.

534
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:31,000
Xaltîk, ... ambêr jîlî no ko, mesela qîzita yê... a xûşke
yeta ye...
 
Aunt, ... let's talk about the generation of today, for
example your daughter... or your sister...

535
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:38,000
Bera dibe ev barge di vî tiştî bacl mînim. Em bîn qa
navîçine... cûnîk bike... ma ne vi tişto jbîr nabê...
 
She says I want to leave this load in this thing. I don't
want to make embroidery... let the young one do it... I
won't forget these things...

536
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:40,000
Tiza... t tişta bargehî a bacl mîne...
 
You know... you teach the things of the load...

537
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:56,000
E barge na be almina, xa aqilê xu nah der sere vî tişno
gi... ekê çik we alminî, noko qîze mê, ê qizê birayê me,
debê, na na, vî şixla xas bi tekemarê nîn beke, hati mazi
bkim... wazê ba we alminm... aze ruk rûbisti basxîza mi yak,
afnavê wina bzonu xartik, xuça dkine.
 
If they don't learn it, they don't put their minds to all
these things... if they learn a little, now our daughter,
our brother's daughter, says, no no, I want to do this
special work, let me do it... I want to learn it... I sit
with our daughter, let her know these things aunt, let her
do whatever she does.

538
00:36:56,000 --> 00:37:07,000
Xo ca dkinen. Qaş paral qobikm dorbkm xu din bmro amkalki dn
pîşi xo. Wadin bîla we almê dekirak bem jêbika xermbla
walaman nawa? Ê wela wa almên arî.
 
Let her do whatever she does. So I can sweep around a
little, let me see an old woman behind me. Then let her
learn, to make an embroidery, learn the embroidery, won't
she? Yes, she learns.

539
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:13,000
A makinc sa er de kalondin, bi baroşoba qibqib made
kalondin, am di mirin. Ma urxan grî di dun...
 
We used to boil clothes on the fire, in big pots, bubbling,
we would die. We would wash heavy quilts...

540
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:17,000
A konî we cem ne ko, urxan maduna b kî xwa debê arê urxan
awdes abiba.
 
And now at this time, we wash the quilts, who among you says
yes, take the quilt to the bathroom.

541
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Ê amna komern ser şîba.
 
And we put the covers on the bed.

542
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:19,000
Şîv.
 
Dinner.

543
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:24,000
Bêr ew şîv mesela... amben şîvet nof dar lagundê ka ferdê
lik.
 
In the past that dinner for example... we say the dinners
were famous in the village of Kafer Dalik.

544
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:25,000
Çina?
 
What?

545
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:35,000
Ê şîvê nuvdar, ista aabîn ma ban evan kê kro? Mçdkr? Madi
kqexojerj krma pe gêrmek xor zêr firik osalat oki xuçedkir.
 
Well, famous dinners, now they say who made these? What did
we do? We roasted a rooster, with bulgur and oil, and
freekeh, and salad, and whatever she made.

546
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:45,000
Ê noko sivra jibra hato daran den taha modudidnan ser. Barê
we nivane u wî şîvî ortoxalo qnaetka, rinda... îhtiramka, j
we dikîra ma zer dikir dînû serwê sfirê.
 
And now they bring the tablecloth from the trees, they put
ten models on it. In the past, that guest and that dinner,
the middle class was content, it's good... respect, from
that rooster we roasted and put on that tablecloth.

547
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:48,000
Yanê dîk serekê bî bvan kibo toçon.
 
I mean, the rooster was the main dish with these foods.

548
00:37:48,000 --> 00:38:08,000
Ê... kûfta dikerin ma, me şparak dekern ma semsok dkerin,
samsoke rzê me derkren kufte dekern... Ee daq noka wa işnogî
tnana..qa xarhat naken gî cêz tînen û hazir dikenu dardekun.
 
Yes... we made meatballs, we made pastries, we made semsok
(a type of pastry), we made rice semsok, we made
meatballs... Well, now none of these things exist.. they
don't bother, they bring everything ready-made and set it
out.

549
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:23,000
Belê.. xoltîk am perst depola mdomo... damet emor gotî ljil
û barge xota jacîraqê honîyê.. ez dexozom basewe ve tiştî
bikim ça ferq mobeyne jl û barge êfrîn o ce îraqî wahaya ? O
çîxtê te çû îraqê... begom.
 
Yes.. aunt, we ask a question... when you said your clothes
are brought from Iraq.. I want to talk about this, what is
the difference between the clothes of Afrin and Iraq? And
when did you go to Iraq... tell me.

550
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Welleh salê du hezar û pênc, ez û apê min va em çûn Îraqê.
Cem lawekî xwe.
 
By God, in the year two thousand and five, my uncle and I
went to Iraq. To one of our sons.

551
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:42,000
Em çûn derê, ma sekir, pey me da na... ronî bû, me kirî ye,
me pê em hatin Efrîn, me anî pir şa bûn, û hawa li cîranan
gotin taşko ne ye mi got, na welleh tiştên Efrîn ne... evê
Iraqê ye...
 
We went there, we looked, after us no... it was bright, we
bought it, we came to Afrin with it, we brought it and they
were very happy, and the neighbors asked what is it, I said,
no by God it's not things from Afrin... this is from Iraq...

552
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:45,000
Me anî tin, bi ro jî ev kar mane cî derketin a.
 
We brought them, and per day these things were sent out from
the place.

553
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:50,000
Ê Efrîn noka ew jî derketin a, wekî derketin a. Bes ne wekî
ya Îraqê. Îraqê başqe bû...
 
Yes, Afrin now has also come out, like they have come out.
But not like the one from Iraq. Iraq was different...

554
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:57,000
Ew du hezar û pênca da çû j'Îraqê anî û derxe kir û... heta
noka ji me re, de tenê ew anî, de ti tiştan dî tune...
 
He went to Iraq in two thousand and five and brought it and
sent it out and... until now for us, he only brought that,
there are no other things...

555
00:38:57,000 --> 00:38:59,000
Me ew bi tenê anîbû welleh.
 
We only brought that, by God.

556
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:07,000
Bes, mehbûc hebûn li derê, qederê tiştan ne wekî wilo ya...
mil bi re, ya kû wî ba, we pir rind a... ko bir bî we...
 
But, there were loved ones there, a lot of things are not
like that... shoulders with, the one that was there, was
very beautiful... who took it...

557
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:11,000
Na wekî ya Îraqê bû. Îraqê ko bar bi rind bû.
 
Not like the one from Iraq. The one from Iraq was very
beautiful.

558
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:12,000
Ez sipasiya te dikim xaltîk.
 
I thank you, aunt.

559
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:14,000
Ya helam sehlen.
 
You are very welcome.

560
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:21,000
Şad û tixtir û xweş. Xêr û silamet be li ser serê me. Bi ser
çavên me. Em pir şa bûn. Sax û selamet bin.
 
Happy and healthy and good. May goodness and health be upon
our heads. Upon our eyes. We were very happy. Stay healthy
and safe.

561
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:41,000
Ya helam sehlen. Şeva we rûn. Hatina we rûn.
 
You are very welcome. Your night is bright. Your coming is
bright.

562
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:02,000
Dest pê kem te nas bikim?
 
Let me start by getting to know you?

563
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Navê min Dilyar Elî ye, ez ji Kaferdelê Jêrîn im, navçeya
Cindirêsê.
 
My name is Dilyar Ali, I am from Lower Kaferdele, Jindires
district.

564
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:08,000
Çend salî ye?
 
How old are you?

565
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:10,000
Ez 17 salî me.
 
I am 17 years old.

566
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:19,000
Wekî we dîtîye ku xwişka kîna ku bi me re li vederê heye, û
tembûr di destê wê de ye û stirana dibêje, ko em ê guhdarîyê
jê bikin bi me re bimînin.
 
As you have seen, our sister who is here with us, and the
tembur is in her hand and she sings, we will listen to her,
stay with us.

567
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Xwe, meraqa dekem min pir hebû inno weleh ew bi aleman û
dar... Xweş li min wan gilîya dikirin.
 
Well, I had a great passion for it, that wow, this
instrument... It sounded good to me.

568
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Xwesiya ez jî balemim (fêr bibim), piştî 7 sala xalê min ji
min re tembûr kirrî.
 
I wished I could learn it too, after 7 years my uncle bought
me a tembur.

569
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:41,000
Vêca min got yella ez ê balemim, dema ez li dest xwe dikim,
wekî pê hest dikim inno tiştekî wisa wek tûrasê me ye. Inno
nizanim yanî...
 
So I said alright I will learn it, when I put my hand on it,
I feel like it's a part of our heritage. Like I don't
know...

570
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:43,000
Tu xwe tê de dibînî yanî bi tembûrê re.
 
You see yourself in it, I mean with the tembur.

571
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:57,000
Erê yanî... Min got ez ê balemim û aqilê min yanî, meraqa
min li ser hebû. Pir meraqa min li ser hebû, min lê dixit,
ez balemîm (fêr bûm) 2 sala. Cema mamoste Elî Îsa, mehdî
adîk (peymangeh) li şêx meqsûd ez balemîm.
 
Yes... I said I will learn it and my mind... I had a passion
for it. I had a lot of passion for it, I played it, I
learned for 2 years. With teacher Ali Isa, at the Adi
Institute in Sheikh Maqsoud I learned.

572
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:58,000
Û hawe feterin hem min qîta kir û niha ko dîsa ez lê dixim,
elhemdulillah.
 
And like that for a period I stopped and now I am playing
again, thank God.

573
00:40:58,000 --> 00:41:00,000
Te tevlî fîstîvala û haflata (ahêng) û dera holê xistîye?
 
Did you participate in festivals, parties, and such?

574
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:05,000
Na ahênga gundê me, gundê me. Ahêngên çêdikî, ez xwe ro (ji
xwe re) derdixim. Wekî din na.
 
No, parties in our village, our village. The parties they
organize, I perform in them. Other than that, no.

575
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:25,000
Hiz bikim dil bi dil têrîn e... Efrîn hat çû xema xweşa...
Herîrê sor o qalo qirşa... Efrîn hat çû xema xweşa... Herîrê
sor o qalo qirşa...
 
(Singing)

576
00:41:31,000 --> 00:41:46,000
Xeberek hatî ji yara min da... Dibên efrîna min e xwaşa...
(Dikenin) Ebo cemidîm we.
 
(Singing)

577
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:52,000
Saxî xweş, gelekî spas, gelekî xweşbû, saeta te xweş.
 
Bless you, thank you very much, it was very beautiful, bless
you.

578
00:41:52,000 --> 00:42:12,000
[Music playing]
 
[Music playing]

579
00:42:48,000 --> 00:43:05,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, niha em hatine vê meydanê, li pişt
min, ciwanên vî gundî bi topê dilîzin, bi lîstika topê, li
vê derê weke fariqekî çêkirine, ko em ê bi hev re derbasî
cem wan bibin, û em ê sekên (binihêrin) ew çawa dilîzin, û
çi zehmetîyê dikşînin. Ko bi me re derbas bin, kerem kin.
 
Yes, dear viewers, now we have come to this square, behind
me, the youth of this village are playing football, the game
of football, here they have formed a team, let's go over to
them together, and we will see how they play, and what
difficulties they face. Come with us, please.

580
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:25,000
[Music playing - people playing football]
 
[Music playing - people playing football]

581
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:43,000
Merheba mamoste.
 
Hello teacher.

582
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:44,000
Ehlan wa sehlan ansê.
 
Welcome miss.

583
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:46,000
Em dikin te nas bikin û te tebixêr (tu bi xêr hatî).
 
We want to get to know you and welcome.

584
00:43:46,000 --> 00:43:52,000
Navê min Mihemed Murad Bekîr bave Şêro. Ez endamek ji
endamên gund im, û idarîyê nadîyê Kaferdalê da bûm berê vê.
 
My name is Mohammed Murad Bekir, father of Shero. I am a
member of the village, and I was an administrator in the
Kaferdele club before this.

585
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:53,000
Spas mamoste.
 
Thank you teacher.

586
00:43:53,000 --> 00:43:57,000
Mamoste em dixwazin behsa dîroka nadîyê bikin. Çi çend sal e
ferîq hat çêkirin li vî gundî de...
 
Teacher, we want to talk about the history of the club. How
many years has the team been formed in this village...

587
00:43:57,000 --> 00:44:14,000
Welleh ferîq yanî em biçûk bûn, ferîqê gund hebû, em alaa
mîstewa gundan dilîstin. Teqrîben di 83, 84an da, bi şiklê
fermî yanî, em alaa mîstewa batulêt Efrînê, gundan da,
destpê bû.
 
Well, the team, I mean we were young, the village team
existed, we played at the village level. Approximately in
83, 84, officially, we started at the level of Afrin
tournaments, among villages.

588
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:33,000
Û gundê me tê da moşarik bû, hin ji wan ew ê biçûk bûn. Û pê
re çû, heta salên 2010an, me ferîqek ala mîstewa Efrînê
mezin me çêkir. Tebêen dimnî Efrînê me dilîst, em û ferîqê
Efrînê bûn, edî ehlî Efrînê bûn, û 3-4 salan yanî em ala tim
minafis bûn.
 
And our village participated in it, some of them were young.
And it went on, until the year 2010, we formed a big team at
the Afrin level. Of course we played within Afrin, it was us
and the Afrin team, the Afrin natives, and for 3-4 years we
were always competing.

589
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:34,000
Ji me eşbal hebûn naci'în hebûn... Yanî xetwat pir xwaş bû
yanî ji me re.
 
We had youth teams, juniors... I mean it was a very good
step for us.

590
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:38,000
Êy destpêkê fariq çêkirin... Kê bîr anî navê gundê we çi bû?
Çend kes bû?
 
Ah, initially forming the team... Who remembered what the
name of your village was? How many people were there?

591
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:58,000
Pir bûn, cem me ji gundê me. Luqman Genc hebû. Mihemed Hesen
hebû. Belê. Cem me, Xelîl Evdelhenan hebû, em ê navê wan gî
diha bînin. Arif Îboş hebû, Mistefa Îboş hebû. Teqrîben
Eynat Îboş hebû, Nedîm Bakîr hebû. Yanî em navê wan gî diha
tînin, ew ê mezin ku dilîstin, di 84 û 85an da, û pê re
zêdetir şebaban em bûn, em bi wan re tiwawir dibûn
(pêşdiketin) em bûn.
 
There were many, from our village. Luqman Genc was there.
Mohammed Hasan was there. Yes. With us, Khalil Avdalhanan
was there, we will mention all their names. Arif Ibosh was
there, Mustafa Ibosh was there. Approximately Aynat Ibosh
was there, Nadim Bakir was there. I mean we mention all
their names, the older ones who played, in 84 and 85, and
then more youth joined us, we developed with them.

592
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:08,000
Em ê, em ê behsa ferîq bikin, ji 2010an û ha ya nah...
 
We will, we will talk about the team, from 2010 and until
now...

593
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:28,000
2010an wextê... mişkilê Efrînê ev bûn, cem me nisbet şebaban
pir bû, cem me kaptin Rêbar heye, ewe Yûvan (Îvan)... Rêbar
Elî, yanî bi xetwakî tabe'en bi îdarîyê meclîsê Efrînê re
dan kir û got em ê nadîyekî çêbikin. Û me jî em pêlekî (bi
hev re) sekînin (sekinîn), cem me la'ibîn (lîstikvan) hebûn
li Efrînê dilîstin, kaptin Ciwan hebû, kaptin Nazmî hebû...
 
In 2010 when... the problems of Afrin occurred, we had a
high percentage of youth, we have captain Rebar, that's
Ivan... Rebar Ali, I mean with a step, of course, consulting
with the administration of the Afrin council and said we
will form a club. And we also stood together, we had players
who played in Afrin, captain Ciwan was there, captain Nazmi
was there...

594
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:54,000
Weke mamosteyê Rêzgar hebû. Û cem me jîlek biçûk hebû, yanî
em pêş ketin û yawaş yawaş, gava me, dengê me pir derket, ji
Efrînê ala mistawa Efrînê, û menteqet muharer.
 
Like teacher Rezgar was there. And we had a young
generation, I mean we advanced and slowly, our step, our
voice became very prominent, from Afrin at the Afrin level,
and the liberated areas.

595
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:56,000
Heta salî şûnî (sala bîrî) salî şûnî êdî nadî Efrîn hat
Heleb, hatin Efrînê, û teqrîben em gî zimnê (di nava) gund
da bûn yanî.
 
Until last year, last year then the Afrin club came to
Aleppo, they came to Afrin, and approximately we were all
within the village.

596
00:45:56,000 --> 00:45:58,000
Tu dimam nadî, hawe hebû..
 
You were always in the club, there was...

597
00:45:58,000 --> 00:45:58,000
Tayîp (baş e), ala mistewa Efrînê, em kanin bêjin, inno
nadîyê Kaferdelê derket, ferîqê Kaferdelê... Te carî betûle
bir?
 
The club... is basically Afrin's, basically we stayed in the
village. And in our village, we organized local tournaments
ourselves, local, I mean a bit for entertainment, going out.

598
00:45:58,000 --> 00:46:01,000
Tayîp (baş e), ala mistewa Efrînê, em kanin bêjin, inno
nadîyê Kaferdelê derket, ferîqê Kaferdelê... Te carî betûle
bir?
 
Okay, at the Afrin level, can we say that the Kaferdele club
emerged, the Kaferdele team... Did you ever win a
tournament?

599
00:46:01,000 --> 00:46:21,000
Me batûle, ew ê berê ê şebab me bir, û ê naşî'în naqilkirî
me bir, û merkezîtiyê cihekî me bir... Havê kîjan salê da
bû? Heve berî vê bi 3 salan, û sala şûnî batûle ê şûhedayê,
şûhedayê Sewra... me Kaferdelê batûle bir. Û ferîqên hebûn
ji pir mekin (xurt) bûn, ruxmê zalîk me batûle bir yanî...
 
We won a tournament, the former youth one we won, and the
transferred juniors one we won, and centralized in one place
we won... Which year was this? This was 3 years before this,
and last year the tournament of the martyrs, the martyrs of
the Revolution... we Kaferdele won the tournament. And there
were teams that were very strong, despite that we won the
tournament...

600
00:46:31,000 --> 00:46:35,000
Sala şûnî pîs, fatreyê me nadîyê Efrîn şêkirî (çêkirî), me
ezmakî pir dît, taba'an daîmîn ji me re hebûn, ji me re
hawedikir qaçkî derve hebûn, weke din muesessat hebûn yanî.
Û ji ehlê gund û idarîyan me pir yanî em, me cefa dît yanî.
 
Last year unfortunately, the period we formed the Afrin
club, we saw a lot of suffering, of course we had
supporters, people who supported us from outside, otherwise
there were institutions. And from the village people and the
administrators, we saw a lot of struggle.

601
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:37,000
Serkeftin be. Saet xweş. Saet te xweş.
 
Good luck. Bless you. Bless you.

602
00:46:37,000 --> 00:46:57,000
[Music playing]
 
[Music playing]

603
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:46,000
Belê, temaşevanên hêja, niha em gihîştin dawîya xeleka
bernameya xwe, bernameya Gund û Welat. Ji gundê Kaferdelê a
Jêrîn, ez im pêşkêşvana we Hac Ehmed, bi hêviya dîtinê, û
xatirê we dixwazim.
 
Yes, dear viewers, now we have reached the end of the
episode of our program, the Village and Country program.
From the village of Lower Kaferdele, I am your host Haj
Ahmed, hoping to see you, and I say goodbye.

